      "text": "Let $ X = \\bigcup\\_{i=2}^{6}\\{A_{i-3}, A_{i-2}\\}$, where  $A_{-i}$ is the element $i$ units clockwise of $A\\_i $, $A\\_0$ is $A\\_i$. We have $|X|=6$ .\nSince $TT^2=I $ $TT^2 \\in X$ and $T \\neq N$ (where N is the set of all Null elements), $T=\\bigcup _{i=1}^2 X\\_i$ and $X\\_i \\neq N \\text{ for all }  i \\in \\{1,2\\}$.\nSo by De Morgan's law,\n$$N=\\bigcap_{i=1}^2 X\\_i^c = \\bigcup_{i=3}^4 X\\_i \\cup \\bigcup_{i=5}^6 X\\_i $$\n\nGiven that $TT^2 =T$ ,\n\n$$TT^2 \\in (X\\_1 \\cup  X\\_4)  \\cap (X\\_2 \\cup  X\\_5) \\cap \\ldots \\cap ( X\\_{ \\frac{9}{2} }\\cap X_{ \\frac{10}{2}} )   $$\n $$TT^2 \\in X\\_2\\cap X\\_4  \\cap \\ldots \\cap X\\_8 \\cap X\\_1 \\downarrow \\bigcap_{i= 2}^8 X\\_i^c  \\equiv S$$\nSo $|S- \\{A\\_2, A\\_6\\}| = |S- \\{A\\_3\\}| + |S- \\{A\\_5\\}| =6-2=4 $ .\n\nThus there are $4^6 \\cdot 3 / 4 = 4320$ ways to arrange them around the polygon.",
